description:
WHY: loomrefinements.md §Acceptance scenarios: "Do not call … a browser build proof of workspace attachment"; "Angular URL", "concurrent browser and agent edits", "browser security" and "several workspaces" need real browser evidence.

GROUNDING:
- No Playwright or Cypress is installed in Tools/loom/node_modules or apps/designer/node_modules.
- %LOCALAPPDATA%\ms-playwright\b holds 18 browser entries, with an unknown version match.
- The only global package is @playwright/mcp@0.0.83 (measured 11:50:25Z).

CHANGE:
- Declare @playwright/test in apps/designer, in its own lockfile. Use the cached chromium if its version matches; otherwise install it per decision 6b.
- The end-to-end test starts the real MCP server over stdio, opens a workspace through loom.workspace and loads viewUrl. It asserts:
  - the actual model is shown, not the sample;
  - every tab renders;
  - concurrent edits by the browser and the agent: one wins, and the stale draft survives with its conflict;
  - a wrong Origin and an expired token are refused;
  - a disconnect gives the offline snapshot;
  - two workspaces in two tabs never retarget each other.

AREA TESTS: from apps/designer, npx playwright test.
WORKER: Sonnet, fresh.
